      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T16:07:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on past conversations with you and Greg, the write swizzle is dependent upon the format of the image, which is pipeline-dependent. So I would at least expect unique pipelines for each write swizzle. \n\nAs far as shaders go, I do think a unique one per each different write swizzle is appropriate (there aren\u0027t many variations). We currently get unique shaders for, say, different output coverages, right? In `SkShaderCodeDictionary::toSkSL(...)`, where we apply the coverage value? I imagine it would be similar to how we handle that. Checking my understanding there.",
      "parentUuid": "51f20c9e_11a2d787",
      "revId": "a247b7484b304c6bc872e38fbabafaa165cace80",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b72efd92_c873f521",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T17:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fragment coverage is pretty fundamentally complex for and can vary a whole lot for \ndifferent geometry (e.g. see\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/gpu/graphite/render/AnalyticRRectRenderStep.cpp;l\u003d781;drc\u003d94d454a12e68f867d0d883900e74f8ffa5a1f6f0 vs https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/gpu/graphite/render/BitmapTextRenderStep.cpp;l\u003d85;drc\u003d15a8ebfde20a034433101582a919e8c530a7a97b) \n\nI\u0027m not sure it\u0027s really comparable to a write swizzle?\n\nIf we already emit a totally different shader for different image types, then I guess it\u0027s fine (that would make this 1:1 on shader count). I just want to avoid going back to the Ganesh mindset where any minute change to a paint would emit new shaders.",
      "parentUuid": "b3033302_be13d741",
      "revId": "a247b7484b304c6bc872e38fbabafaa165cace80",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fb504a4_f038d345",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
