      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T18:01:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, this is a pretty small change in terms of the actual SkSL, but can result in very different colored image outputs (as you can probably imagine). I guess I\u0027m not entirely clear on how one would capture different write swizzles within the scope of one unique shader. I would also like to avoid that Ganesh trap if we can avoid it. :) \n\nIs there an example you could point me to of different behavior being captured within one unique shader? I\u0027m not positive if we *do* already emit a totally different shader for different image types.",
      "parentUuid": "b72efd92_c873f521",
